# Future Single-Player Platformer

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Post-vertical-slice expansion
Dependencies: Approved EntropyTag vertical slice and explicit mode preproduction

## Purpose

Develop an original single-player mode that broadens EntropyTag beyond competitive territory matches through
comedic, rage-inducing precision platforming.

## Direction

- Use bounce, momentum, timing, and recovery as the traversal foundation.
- Create humor through surprising but readable environmental hostility and slapstick failure.
- Preserve EntropyTag's original world, characters, terminology, levels, art, audio, and mechanics.
- Treat other games only as high-level genre references; do not copy protected expression or proprietary
  content.

## Tasks

- [ ] Define how the mode connects to EntropyTag's elemental identity.
- [ ] Define the core bounce and momentum model.
- [ ] Define failure, recovery, checkpoint, and restart cadence.
- [ ] Prototype one short vertical platforming course.
- [ ] Prototype readable environmental hazards and comedic reactions.
- [ ] Establish difficulty and frustration guardrails.
- [ ] Test keyboard/mouse and gamepad controls.
- [ ] Validate whether the mode should share the competitive player controller.
- [ ] Create an original visual, audio, narrative, and level-design brief.
- [ ] Conduct isolated player testing before production approval.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The mode is mechanically and visually original.
- [ ] Failure feels attributable, fast to recover from, and intentionally funny rather than arbitrary.
- [ ] A short prototype demonstrates satisfying bounce/momentum traversal.
- [ ] The mode has a documented relationship to the main EntropyTag product.
- [ ] Production begins only after the vertical slice is approved.

## Completion evidence

Not completed.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-21 - Future direction recorded from developer feedback. Implementation is explicitly deferred until
  after the main vertical slice.
